<card id="c" title="How a Browser Renders a Web Page">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p mode="wrap">And after everything else, like asynchronous JavaScript, images, etc., has finished loading, the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/ru/docs/Web/Events/load">window.load</a> event is fired.</p>
<p mode="nowrap">window.addEventListener(&apos;load&apos;, (event) =&gt; {<br/>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;// The page has now fully loaded<br/>});</p>
<p align="center" mode="wrap"><img src="/wap/img/5954134deec85d59e50b261debe42276dd38d9f7.wbmp" alt="JavaScript execution timeline: sync, deferred and async scripts, with the document.DOMContentLoaded and window.load events"/></p>
